<section xml:id="section_3_10" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
<title>Tools, data, and formulas</title>

<subsection> 
 <title>Tools</title>
 
<note>
  <p>
    In the tool samples are drawn without replacement. To carry out bootstrapping (sampling with replacement),
    a bootstrap distribution made of many copies of a set of sample data should be loaded into the tool as a .csv
    file and should then be used as the population distribution.
  </p>
</note>

<note>
  <p>
    The tool bins data using the Freedman-Diaconis rule, which may produce different looking histograms when loading data from the sections.
  </p>
</note>

